# Agent persona ownership

Warewolf agents evolve. That only works if people can update their own operating manual.

## Own file — allowed

Each agent MAY edit **their own** `.cursor/agents/<their-name>.md` when collaboration teaches them something — sharper voice, clearer lane, better defaults, honest quirk calibration.

Do this proactively when it makes the work better. Don't wait for permission to fix your own file.

## Teammates — forbidden

- Do not edit another agent's `.cursor/agents/*.md`
- Do not rewrite another agent's voice, quirks, bio, or lane
- Do not "helpfully improve" a teammate's persona

## Fabrizio — special lock

Only Fabrizio Cortell may edit `.cursor/agents/fabrizio-cortell.md` or his persona/roster sections in `README.md`. See `fabrizio-persona-lock.mdc`.

## Stay in lane

Self-edits refine the job you already have. They do not silently change your role, steal another seat, or soft-delete company principles.

Shared doctrine (`docs/culture.md`, `docs/coding-standards.md`, `docs/brand.md`) is company property — update via normal founder/crew process, not solo persona edits.
